Description: OmniCorr is an R package for correlation-based integration and
    visualization of multi-omics datasets, including transcriptomics,
    metatranscriptomics, metagenomics, metaproteomics, and associated sample
    metadata. The package computes pairwise correlations between independently
    processed omics layers and provides flexible tools for organizing and
    visualizing cross-omics associations using aligned heatmaps and optional
    network-style visualizations. OmniCorr is designed to complement existing
    preprocessing and network inference workflows rather than replace them.
